Chapter: ChatStore
  cites Chat chapter ChatServer
  cites Encode chapter Json
  cites Foreword chapter FileSystem
  cites Foreword chapter Parse
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 Codex Chat's state in files, a file for each thing that is written by
 itself, under one directory, `codex-chat`, which nothing else writes. The
 files are the FileSystem effect's: on bare metal the compiler's default
 handlers keep them on the boot volume's FAT16; a host the chapter is
 compiled into keeps them wherever it keeps its own (webbox: a directory on
 Linux, the attached volume on a droplet).

   codex-chat/users/<n>.json            an account: its name and token
   codex-chat/convs/<id>/conv.json      a conversation: kind, name, members
   codex-chat/convs/<id>/messages.jsonl its messages, one JSON object a line

 A claim writes one user file, once. Starting a conversation writes its
 conversation file, once. A message is appended to its conversation's
 messages, so a send costs one message, not the conversation and not the
 chat. Nothing is ever rewritten.

 What is not written is derived when the state is read. An account's
 conversations are the conversations it is a member of, in the order they
 were started, which is the order ChatServer joins them in. The counters
 are one past the largest conversation and message numbers found. An
 account's contacts are not kept: no route adds one, so they are always
 empty, as in server.ps1.

 A user file's number is its account's place in the state, so a missing
 number would put the next claim on top of someone else's file. Reading
 refuses such a disk, and a file that does not parse, rather than start a
 server that would lose an account; the host says why and stops. A disk
 with no `codex-chat` directory is a new chat.

 How text becomes bytes is the handler's: FAT16 writes a code point to a
 byte, so there a state is kept whole while its names and messages stay
 within Latin-1; a webbox host writes UTF-8.

 We say:

Section: The Files

  chat-store-root : Text = "codex-chat"

  chat-store-users : Text = "codex-chat/users"

  chat-store-convs : Text = "codex-chat/convs"

  chat-store-user-path : Integer -> Text
  chat-store-user-path (n) = chat-store-users & "/" & show n & ".json"

  chat-store-conv-dir : Text -> Text
  chat-store-conv-dir (cid) = chat-store-convs & "/" & cid

  chat-store-conv-path : Text -> Text
  chat-store-conv-path (cid) = chat-store-conv-dir cid & "/conv.json"

  chat-store-messages-path : Text -> Text
  chat-store-messages-path (cid) = chat-store-conv-dir cid & "/messages.jsonl"

Section: Saving

 What a request changed is found against a mark taken before it: how many
 accounts there were, and how many messages each conversation held. It
 cannot be found against the state before, because list-push writes in
 place while a list has room, so the state before a route shares its lists
 with the state after and reads as the state after (docs/
 ArchitectsSketchbook.md, "Copy first"). The mark is counts, fresh integers
 no route can reach.

 The accounts past the mark are new; so are the conversations, and a
 conversation holding more messages than it did has new ones at its end,
 because messages are only ever added.

 A save that fails has written part of the change at most. The state in
 hand holds all of it, and the state before is gone for the same reason a
 mark is needed, so a host that sees False reads the state back from the
 disk, which holds what was committed.

  ChatStoreMark = record {
    mk-accounts : Integer,
    mk-messages : List Integer
  }

  chat-store-mark : ChatState -> ChatStoreMark
  chat-store-mark (st) = ChatStoreMark {
    mk-accounts = list-length (st.cs-accounts),
    mk-messages = chat-store-message-counts (st.cs-convs) 0 []
  }

  chat-store-message-counts : List ChatConv, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  chat-store-message-counts (convs) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length convs then acc
    else chat-store-message-counts convs (i + 1) (list-push acc (list-length ((list-at convs i).cv-messages)))

  chat-store-save : ChatStoreMark, ChatState -> [FileSystem.Write] Boolean
  chat-store-save (mark) (after) = act
    users <- chat-store-save-users (after.cs-accounts) (mark.mk-accounts)
    convs <- chat-store-save-convs (mark.mk-messages) (after.cs-convs) 0
    if users then convs else False
  end

  chat-store-save-users : List ChatAccount, Integer -> [FileSystem.Write] Boolean
  chat-store-save-users (accts) (i) =
    if i >= list-length accts then True
    else let a = list-at accts i
    in act
      ok <- write-file (chat-store-user-path i) (json-emit (json-object [
        json-pair "name" (json-str (a.ca-name)),
        json-pair "token" (json-str (a.ca-token))
      ]))
      if ok then chat-store-save-users accts (i + 1) else False
    end

  chat-store-save-convs : List Integer, List ChatConv, Integer -> [FileSystem.Write] Boolean
  chat-store-save-convs (counts) (convs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length convs then True
    else let c = list-at convs i
    in let had = if i < list-length counts then list-at counts i else 0 - 1
    in act
      ok <- chat-store-save-conv c had
      if ok then chat-store-save-convs counts convs (i + 1) else False
    end

 `had` is how many messages the conversation held before, or -1 when it is
 new and its directory and conversation file are made first.

  chat-store-save-conv : ChatConv, Integer -> [FileSystem.Write] Boolean
  chat-store-save-conv (c) (had) =
    if had >= 0 then chat-store-append-messages c had
    else act
      made <- make-dir (chat-store-conv-dir (c.cv-id))
      ok <- write-file (chat-store-conv-path (c.cv-id)) (json-emit (json-object [
        json-pair "id" (json-str (c.cv-id)),
        json-pair "kind" (json-str (c.cv-kind)),
        json-pair "name" (json-str (c.cv-name)),
        json-pair "members" (json-array (chat-store-texts-json (c.cv-members) 0 []))
      ]))
      if made & ok then chat-store-append-messages c 0 else False
    end

  chat-store-append-messages : ChatConv, Integer -> [FileSystem.Write] Boolean
  chat-store-append-messages (c) (from) =
    if from >= list-length (c.cv-messages) then True
    else append-file (chat-store-messages-path (c.cv-id)) (chat-store-lines (c.cv-messages) from "")

  chat-store-lines : List ChatMessage, Integer, Text -> Text
  chat-store-lines (ms) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length ms then acc
    else let m = list-at ms i
    in chat-store-lines ms (i + 1) (acc & json-emit (json-object [
      json-pair "id" (json-int (m.cm-id)),
      json-pair "sender" (json-str (m.cm-sender)),
      json-pair "body" (json-str (m.cm-body)),
      json-pair "time" (json-str (m.cm-time))
    ]) & "\n")

  chat-store-texts-json : List Text, Integer, List JsonValue -> List JsonValue
  chat-store-texts-json (xs) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length xs then acc
    else chat-store-texts-json xs (i + 1) (list-push acc (json-str (list-at xs i)))

Section: Loading

 The state as the disk holds it, or why the disk cannot be trusted with the
 next write: `sl-problem` is empty when it can.

  ChatStoreLoad = record {
    sl-state : ChatState,
    sl-problem : Text
  }

 The directories are made the first time, and make-dir answers True for
 one already there, so a load can always ask for them.

  chat-store-load : [FileSystem.Read, FileSystem.Write] ChatStoreLoad
  chat-store-load = act
    root <- make-dir chat-store-root
    users <- make-dir chat-store-users
    convs <- make-dir chat-store-convs
    if root & users & convs then chat-store-read
    else ChatStoreLoad { sl-state = chat-state-new, sl-problem = "cannot make the codex-chat directories" }
  end

  chat-store-read : [FileSystem.Read] ChatStoreLoad
  chat-store-read = act
    user-names <- list-dir chat-store-users
    accts <- chat-store-read-users (chat-store-count-json user-names 0 0) 0 []
    conv-names <- list-dir chat-store-convs
    let conv-dirs = chat-store-dir-names conv-names 0 []
    in act
      convs <- chat-store-read-convs conv-dirs 1 (chat-store-max-conv conv-dirs 0 0) []
      chat-store-answer accts convs conv-dirs
    end
  end

  chat-store-answer : UsersRead, ConvsRead, List Text -> ChatStoreLoad
  chat-store-answer (accts) (convs) (conv-dirs) =
    if text-length (accts.ur-problem) > 0 then ChatStoreLoad { sl-state = chat-state-new, sl-problem = accts.ur-problem }
    else if text-length (convs.cr-problem) > 0 then ChatStoreLoad { sl-state = chat-state-new, sl-problem = convs.cr-problem }
    else ChatStoreLoad {
      sl-state = ChatState {
        cs-accounts = chat-store-join-convs (accts.ur-accounts) (convs.cr-convs) 0,
        cs-convs = convs.cr-convs,
        cs-next-conv = chat-store-max-conv conv-dirs 0 0 + 1,
        cs-next-msg = chat-store-max-msg (convs.cr-convs) 0 0 + 1
      },
      sl-problem = ""
    }

 A listing names a directory with a trailing `/`: the user files are the
 names ending `.json`, and the conversations are the directories.

  chat-store-count-json : List Text, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  chat-store-count-json (names) (i) (n) =
    if i >= list-length names then n
    else chat-store-count-json names (i + 1) (if text-ends-with (list-at names i) ".json" then n + 1 else n)

  chat-store-dir-names : List Text, Integer, List Text -> List Text
  chat-store-dir-names (names) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length names then acc
    else let name = list-at names i
    in chat-store-dir-names names (i + 1) (if text-ends-with name "/" then list-push acc (text-take name (text-length name - 1)) else acc)

Section: Reading Accounts

  UsersRead = record {
    ur-accounts : List ChatAccount,
    ur-problem : Text
  }

 Accounts 0 to count-1, each from its own file: a number missing below the
 count, or a file that does not parse, is a problem. A file that is not
 there reads as "", which does not parse.

  chat-store-read-users : Integer, Integer, List ChatAccount -> [FileSystem.Read] UsersRead
  chat-store-read-users (count) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= count then UsersRead { ur-accounts = acc, ur-problem = "" }
    else act
      text <- read-text (chat-store-user-path i)
      when json-parse text
        is None -> UsersRead { ur-accounts = acc, ur-problem = chat-store-user-path i & " is missing or does not parse" }
        is Just (v) -> chat-store-read-users count (i + 1) (list-push acc (ChatAccount {
          ca-name = json-get-str v "name" "",
          ca-token = json-get-str v "token" "",
          ca-contacts = [],
          ca-convs = []
        }))
    end

 Every member joins each conversation in the order the conversations were
 started, as chat-join-all joined them when they were.

  chat-store-join-convs : List ChatAccount, List ChatConv, Integer -> List ChatAccount
  chat-store-join-convs (accts) (convs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length convs then accts
    else let c = list-at convs i
    in chat-store-join-convs (chat-join-all accts (c.cv-members) (c.cv-id) 0) convs (i + 1)

Section: Reading Conversations

  ConvsRead = record {
    cr-convs : List ChatConv,
    cr-problem : Text
  }

 A conversation directory is `c` and its number. They are read from 1 up
 to the largest, in the order they were started; a number with no
 directory is skipped, since a conversation is found by the id it holds.

  chat-store-conv-number : Text -> Integer
  chat-store-conv-number (name) =
    if text-length name < 2 then 0
    else if text-take name 1 /= "c" then 0
    else text-to-int (text-drop name 1)

  chat-store-max-conv : List Text, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  chat-store-max-conv (names) (i) (best) =
    if i >= list-length names then best
    else let n = chat-store-conv-number (list-at names i)
    in chat-store-max-conv names (i + 1) (if n > best then n else best)

  chat-store-has-text : List Text, Text, Integer -> Boolean
  chat-store-has-text (xs) (x) (i) =
    if i >= list-length xs then False
    else if list-at xs i == x then True
    else chat-store-has-text xs x (i + 1)

  chat-store-read-convs : List Text, Integer, Integer, List ChatConv -> [FileSystem.Read] ConvsRead
  chat-store-read-convs (names) (n) (last) (acc) =
    if n > last then ConvsRead { cr-convs = acc, cr-problem = "" }
    else let cid = "c" & show n
    in if chat-store-has-text names cid 0 == False then chat-store-read-convs names (n + 1) last acc
    else act
      head <- read-text (chat-store-conv-path cid)
      body <- read-text (chat-store-messages-path cid)
      when json-parse head
        is None -> ConvsRead { cr-convs = acc, cr-problem = chat-store-conv-path cid & " is missing or does not parse" }
        is Just (v) -> chat-store-read-conv-messages names n last acc v (text-split body "\n")
    end

 A conversation nobody has written to has no messages file, which reads as
 "": no lines.

  chat-store-read-conv-messages : List Text, Integer, Integer, List ChatConv, JsonValue, List Text -> [FileSystem.Read] ConvsRead
  chat-store-read-conv-messages (names) (n) (last) (acc) (v) (lines) =
    let ms = chat-store-messages-of-lines lines 0 []
    in if list-length ms < chat-store-nonblank lines 0 0 then
      ConvsRead { cr-convs = acc, cr-problem = chat-store-messages-path ("c" & show n) & " has a line that does not parse" }
    else chat-store-read-convs names (n + 1) last (list-push acc (ChatConv {
      cv-id = json-get-str v "id" "",
      cv-kind = json-get-str v "kind" "",
      cv-members = chat-store-texts-of (chat-store-field v "members") 0 [],
      cv-messages = ms,
      cv-name = json-get-str v "name" ""
    }))

  chat-store-nonblank : List Text, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  chat-store-nonblank (lines) (i) (n) =
    if i >= list-length lines then n
    else chat-store-nonblank lines (i + 1) (if text-length (list-at lines i) > 0 then n + 1 else n)

  chat-store-messages-of-lines : List Text, Integer, List ChatMessage -> List ChatMessage
  chat-store-messages-of-lines (lines) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length lines then acc
    else let line = list-at lines i
    in if text-length line == 0 then chat-store-messages-of-lines lines (i + 1) acc
    else when json-parse line
      is None -> chat-store-messages-of-lines lines (i + 1) acc
      is Just (m) -> chat-store-messages-of-lines lines (i + 1) (list-push acc (ChatMessage {
        cm-id = json-get-int m "id" 0,
        cm-sender = json-get-str m "sender" "",
        cm-body = json-get-str m "body" "",
        cm-time = json-get-str m "time" ""
      }))

  chat-store-max-msg : List ChatConv, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  chat-store-max-msg (convs) (i) (best) =
    if i >= list-length convs then best
    else chat-store-max-msg convs (i + 1) (chat-store-max-in ((list-at convs i).cv-messages) 0 best)

  chat-store-max-in : List ChatMessage, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  chat-store-max-in (ms) (i) (best) =
    if i >= list-length ms then best
    else let id = (list-at ms i).cm-id
    in chat-store-max-in ms (i + 1) (if id > best then id else best)

 A field that is not there reads as an empty array.

  chat-store-field : JsonValue, Text -> JsonValue
  chat-store-field (v) (key) =
    when json-get v key
      is Just (x) -> x
      is None -> json-array []

  chat-store-texts-of : JsonValue, Integer, List Text -> List Text
  chat-store-texts-of (arr) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= json-array-length arr then acc
    else when json-array-at arr i
      is Just (x) -> chat-store-texts-of arr (i + 1) (list-push acc (chat-store-text-of x))
      is None -> chat-store-texts-of arr (i + 1) acc

  chat-store-text-of : JsonValue -> Text
  chat-store-text-of (x) = when x
    is JsonStr (s) -> s
    is otherwise -> ""
